{"title":"Mill's Constant","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Mill's Constant is defined as the smallest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1aadd9a7b81d0f73ae18a4ae52163458153d967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\theta^{3^n}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"21\" /> is always a prime number for all natural n.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1aadd9a7b81d0f73ae18a4ae52163458153d967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor\\theta^{3^n}\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"21\" /> is the prime number theorem where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be any number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an element from an set of numbers (that may be rational or irrational, and we are not sure) and Mill's Constant is the smallest element in that set. If the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_Hypothesis\" title=\"Riemann Hypothesis\">Riemann Hypothesis</a> is true, Mill's constant is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/c/8dc83d3b6f8c0271169876a2e8e8dde497c00ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3063778838630806904686144926...$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"282\" height=\"13\" /> and the primes it generates start as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe1e3797b438ccc6c638e867fee0d024a13d5bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 11, 1361, 2521008887, 16022236204009818131831320183,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"454\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c23204c229520072b09741623ebed6efa9d12ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4113101149215104800030529537915953170486139623539759933135949994882770404074832568499, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"794\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Mill%27s_Constant&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095558\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 31/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1605/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.623      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.623      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15128:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018095558 and revision id 169911. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}